1
00:00:00,758 --> 00:00:02,713
For most of human history the treatment was words.

2
00:00:02,713 --> 00:00:07,013
Someone who knew the right ones would stand over you and
say them aloud, and that was not superstition at all.

3
00:00:07,013 --> 00:00:09,242
It was simply the state of the art, for a very long time.

4
00:00:10,952 --> 00:00:12,221
It was not a fringe practice.

5
00:00:12,221 --> 00:00:17,166
The Chinese state kept a department of ritual healing on the
imperial medical payroll for about a thousand years,

6
00:00:17,166 --> 00:00:19,048
paid from the same purse as its physicians.

7
00:00:20,503 --> 00:00:24,848
I have heard that the physicians of high antiquity cured a
man by shifting his essence and transforming his breath

8
00:00:24,848 --> 00:00:28,239
with a single invocation, while my own physicians use
poisons inside and needles outside,

9
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:29,497
and it works about half the time.

10
00:00:30,666 --> 00:00:34,667
Notice what he has actually asked, which is not how
medicine works but whether it has got worse,

11
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:39,084
an emperor asking his own physician whether the
profession he pays for has been declining since before his

12
00:00:39,084 --> 00:00:39,335
birth.

13
00:00:40,692 --> 00:00:42,521
The answer is not the one you are braced for.

14
00:00:42,521 --> 00:00:46,341
Nobody in this room is going to tell you that the old
invocations were stronger than a needle.

15
00:00:46,341 --> 00:00:49,308
What changed was not the medicine at all, it was the
patients themselves.

16
00:00:50,361 --> 00:00:55,410
The chapter is Suwen thirteen, from the first half of the
Yellow Emperor's Inner Canon. Its title is four characters,

17
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:59,639
shift the essence and transform the breath, and that is a
fairly good working definition of magic.

18
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:04,765
This is The Emperor's Inner Canon, and the episode is
called When Medicine Stopped Being Magic.

19
00:01:04,765 --> 00:01:09,701
The argument is that the moment is real, that it happens in
this chapter, and that it is not a clean one.

20
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:12,926
Nobody invited me and I am staying. Here is what I am
listening for.

21
00:01:12,926 --> 00:01:15,792
A man is about to explain that the past was better and the
present is worse,

22
00:01:15,792 --> 00:01:19,638
which is the most common thing anybody has ever said
about anything. I want a mechanism, not a memory.

23
00:01:20,769 --> 00:01:24,325
Watch the chapter retire its own inheritance, on the record
and in front of the throne.

24
00:01:24,325 --> 00:01:25,920
Then watch what it reaches for instead,

25
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:29,232
and decide for yourself whether the thing it retired ever
actually left the room.

26
00:01:30,854 --> 00:01:33,353
Here is the sentence you are asking about. In treating
illness,

27
00:01:33,353 --> 00:01:37,401
they had only to shift the essence and transform the breath,
and it could be done by invocation alone,

28
00:01:37,401 --> 00:01:39,147
four characters for method and two for cure.

29
00:01:40,977 --> 00:01:44,813
The word is zhuyou. Zhu means to speak aloud to a power,
and you means the origin.

30
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:49,024
The physician found out where the illness had come from
and then addressed it by its name.

31
00:01:50,579 --> 00:01:51,674
And this was a real office.

32
00:01:51,674 --> 00:01:56,460
Incantation had its own department in the imperial medical
service for about a thousand years, across three dynasties,

33
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:59,422
and the Ming court did not abolish it until the year fifteen
seventy-one.

34
00:02:00,975 --> 00:02:05,359
Then I am funding it. There is a bureau in my medical
service whose officers are paid to know the right words,

35
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:09,025
and you are about to tell me in front of them that the words
have stopped working, so go on.

36
00:02:10,637 --> 00:02:14,936
I am going to tell you something more awkward than that.
The practitioner did not fight the illness.

37
00:02:14,936 --> 00:02:19,363
He established where it had come from and he said so out
loud, and the saying was the entire treatment.

38
00:02:20,892 --> 00:02:25,111
Hold on to the shape of that, because it is not what people
assume. The target is not the body.

39
00:02:25,111 --> 00:02:29,109
The target is the account of how the illness got there,
corrected out loud to the patient.

40
00:02:30,757 --> 00:02:34,296
First finding, and it is not the one you expect from me. If a
state pays for something for a thousand years,

41
00:02:34,296 --> 00:02:37,998
it is usually because it appears to work often enough to
keep the receipts coming. I am not going to laugh at it.

42
00:02:37,998 --> 00:02:39,243
I want to know which part was working.

43
00:02:40,741 --> 00:02:42,777
That is a fair question and it has a real answer.

44
00:02:42,777 --> 00:02:46,434
Ritual and expectation and undivided attention have
measurable effects on a sick person,

45
00:02:46,434 --> 00:02:49,259
and this has been studied carefully and is not seriously in
dispute.

46
00:02:50,919 --> 00:02:55,914
What they move is how illness is experienced. Reported
pain and nausea and exhaustion can shift on ritual alone,

47
00:02:55,914 --> 00:02:59,081
sometimes a great deal, and that shift is real to the person
having it.

48
00:03:00,878 --> 00:03:02,450
What they do not move is the disease.

49
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:06,870
The tumour is the same size afterwards and the fracture is
not knitted and the infection is not cleared,

50
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:09,122
and nothing here should be heard as saying otherwise.

51
00:03:10,981 --> 00:03:15,812
And the remarkable thing is that we are not correcting the
chapter here. The chapter is about to say this itself,

52
00:03:15,812 --> 00:03:19,019
in its own words, and it is going to say it rather harder than
we just did.

53
00:03:20,793 --> 00:03:24,683
In the old time, people lived among the birds and the
beasts, and that is the whole setting.

54
00:03:24,683 --> 00:03:29,207
No walls are mentioned and no granary and no physician,
and the chapter does not think anything is missing.

55
00:03:30,613 --> 00:03:35,112
They moved about in order to avoid the cold, and stayed in
shaded places in order to avoid the heat.

56
00:03:35,112 --> 00:03:39,387
Two clauses for an entire way of living, and both of them
are about staying out of the weather.

57
00:03:41,018 --> 00:03:44,648
Read it exactly as it is written. It is not a claim about virtue
and it is not a claim about diet.

58
00:03:44,648 --> 00:03:48,982
It is a claim about exposure to the weather, and about how
much of that exposure these people could actually control.

59
00:03:50,711 --> 00:03:53,890
So far this is a golden age, and every culture on earth has
one of those.

60
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:56,851
What makes this chapter different arrives in the very next
sentence,

61
00:03:56,851 --> 00:03:59,290
and it is the reason the whole argument survives at all.

62
00:04:00,645 --> 00:04:03,535
Within them there was no burden of longing and no weight of
attachment.

63
00:04:03,535 --> 00:04:06,954
Outside them there was no shape of striving after office.
Those are the two clauses,

64
00:04:06,954 --> 00:04:09,356
and everything the chapter claims afterwards rests on them.

65
00:04:10,845 --> 00:04:13,737
That is a psychological claim, and it is doing all of the
work.

66
00:04:13,737 --> 00:04:19,156
The mechanism is not clean air and it is not a simple diet.
It is the absence of wanting things, for a whole lifetime.

67
00:04:21,012 --> 00:04:25,517
No longing and no ambition. Physician, you have described
a man with nothing to hope for and no post to lose,

68
00:04:25,517 --> 00:04:28,988
and held him up to me as the healthy one. I built my entire
court from the opposite.

69
00:04:30,742 --> 00:04:31,919
I have held nothing up to you.

70
00:04:31,919 --> 00:04:35,137
I am describing the conditions under which a spoken
sentence was enough treatment.

71
00:04:35,137 --> 00:04:39,258
Whether those conditions were pleasant to live in is another
question, and the chapter does not raise it.

72
00:04:40,973 --> 00:04:45,569
This was an age of calm, the chapter says, and the evil
could not enter deeply. That phrase is the hinge,

73
00:04:45,569 --> 00:04:49,028
because it does not say the evil was absent, only that it
could not get in far.

74
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:55,334
And so, the chapter says, poisons could not treat their
inside and needles and stones could not treat their outside.

75
00:04:55,334 --> 00:04:59,220
It was enough to shift the essence and speak to the origin.
That is the whole ancient prescription.

76
00:05:00,348 --> 00:05:05,230
Read that clause again, because almost everyone reads it
wrong. It does not say the ancients had no drugs.

77
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:09,652
It says that drugs could not treat them, which is a different
and a much stranger claim to make.

78
00:05:11,049 --> 00:05:15,678
There was nothing deep enough in them for a drug to reach.
The spell was sufficient because the illness was shallow,

79
00:05:15,678 --> 00:05:18,951
and that is a mechanism with a real shape, which means
that it can be argued with.

80
00:05:20,321 --> 00:05:21,899
Second finding, and it is a real argument.

81
00:05:21,899 --> 00:05:26,071
It has a mechanism and it makes a prediction and you could
check it, which is more than most nostalgia manages.

82
00:05:26,071 --> 00:05:29,679
I came in expecting to catch a man missing the old days,
and he handed me something falsifiable.

83
00:05:30,435 --> 00:05:34,176
The present age is not like this. Worry and grief wind
around a man from the inside,

84
00:05:34,176 --> 00:05:39,566
and hard labour and exhaustion injure him from the outside.
Both arrive from the life he is living, not from the weather.

85
00:05:41,064 --> 00:05:44,941
Two causes, one inside and one outside, and both of them
are social. Nobody has mentioned a demon.

86
00:05:44,941 --> 00:05:48,936
The chapter has moved the cause of illness out of the spirit
world and into the conditions of a life.

87
00:05:50,488 --> 00:05:55,084
They have also lost their compliance with the four seasons
and gone against what is fitting for cold and heat.

88
00:05:55,084 --> 00:05:59,513
Thief winds arrive again and again, and hollow evils come
morning and evening, and no season escapes them.

89
00:06:00,872 --> 00:06:04,621
The thief wind and the hollow evil are old words for an
ordinary idea, which is exposure.

90
00:06:04,621 --> 00:06:09,128
What changed is not the wind itself but how much of it
reaches a person already worn through by their life.

91
00:06:10,663 --> 00:06:13,996
Inside, it reaches as far as the five organs and the marrow
of the bones,

92
00:06:13,996 --> 00:06:16,233
and outside it damages the openings and the skin.

93
00:06:16,233 --> 00:06:19,338
So a small illness becomes severe and a great illness ends
in death.

94
00:06:20,834 --> 00:06:25,320
And therefore the invocation cannot bring it to an end. That
is the chapter speaking, not a later critic.

95
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:29,166
The tradition's own foundational text is retiring its own
inheritance, in a single clause.

96
00:06:30,601 --> 00:06:35,365
Six characters say that therefore the invocation cannot end
it. That is the sentence this episode is named for,

97
00:06:35,365 --> 00:06:39,399
and it was written by people who had every reason to keep
the old method exactly where it was.

98
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:43,918
I asked why my physicians fail, and you have answered me
with my own court.

99
00:06:43,918 --> 00:06:46,342
The worry is mine and the striving after office is mine,

100
00:06:46,342 --> 00:06:49,330
and the men who are worn out in my service are all on my
own payroll.

101
00:06:50,555 --> 00:06:53,963
Third finding, and now I am less impressed. Every age in
this chapter looks back at a better one.

102
00:06:53,963 --> 00:06:57,899
The present envies the middle age and the middle age
envies high antiquity and high antiquity is too far back to

103
00:06:57,899 --> 00:06:59,446
check. That is a ladder with no bottom rung.

104
00:07:00,373 --> 00:07:02,872
He is half right, so score him in two separate halves.

105
00:07:02,872 --> 00:07:06,203
Long-term worry really does affect immunity and the health
of the heart,

106
00:07:06,203 --> 00:07:09,627
and counting grief among the causes of illness is not at all
a naive idea.

107
00:07:10,618 --> 00:07:13,467
The other half fails. There was never an age without deep
disease.

108
00:07:13,467 --> 00:07:16,878
Bones from every period we can dig up carry infection and
tumour and arthritis,

109
00:07:16,878 --> 00:07:19,382
and the peaceful age of this chapter is a literary device.

110
00:07:20,881 --> 00:07:25,356
So the chapter has just retired the method it inherited. The
interesting question is what it reaches for instead,

111
00:07:25,356 --> 00:07:29,119
and the answer turns out to be the single most important
thing in the whole of this short text.

112
00:07:30,962 --> 00:07:34,515
Then let us have it. I want to stand before a sick man and
see whether he lives or dies,

113
00:07:34,515 --> 00:07:39,039
and settle a doubt where two of my physicians disagree,
and I want the essentials made as plain as the sunlight.

114
00:07:40,929 --> 00:07:44,761
Colour and pulse are what the high sovereign valued and
what the teachers before me handed down.

115
00:07:44,761 --> 00:07:49,072
Two instruments, and the chapter names them in that order
and never adds a third for the rest of its length.

116
00:07:50,816 --> 00:07:54,163
Notice where the authority has moved. Not to a spirit and
not to a revelation,

117
00:07:54,163 --> 00:07:59,184
but to what the teachers before her handed down, which is a
lineage of people who could each be named and questioned.

118
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:05,757
In high antiquity the sovereign set Jiu Dai-ji to the work.
He put colour and pulse in order and so reached clarity,

119
00:08:05,757 --> 00:08:09,563
matching them against wood and fire and earth and metal
and water, and the seasons.

120
00:08:10,368 --> 00:08:14,278
The canon almost never names anybody, and it names him
here. That is not decoration.

121
00:08:14,278 --> 00:08:19,632
A chapter about method is telling you that the method has a
human teacher rather than a source somewhere in heaven.

122
00:08:20,768 --> 00:08:25,154
Matched also to the four seasons and the eight winds and
the six directions, never departing from their constants.

123
00:08:25,154 --> 00:08:29,232
Then watch how the changes move against each other, so
the small things are seen and the essentials known.

124
00:08:30,647 --> 00:08:34,372
That list is a grid, and the grid is the point. A reading
means nothing on its own.

125
00:08:34,372 --> 00:08:39,353
It only means something against what it should have been
at this particular season and at this particular hour.

126
00:08:40,461 --> 00:08:43,118
Colour answers to the sun and the pulse answers to the
moon.

127
00:08:43,118 --> 00:08:48,343
Seek the essentials constantly and you will have them. The
changes of colour answer to the pulses of the four seasons,

128
00:08:48,343 --> 00:08:49,539
which the sovereign valued.

129
00:08:51,071 --> 00:08:55,397
The image is better than it sounds. Colour is what you take
in at a glance, whole and all at once.

130
00:08:55,397 --> 00:08:58,930
Pulse moves in phases under your fingers, and you have to
wait for it to arrive.

131
00:09:00,805 --> 00:09:03,183
Fourth finding, and this one I like. Look where these
instruments are.

132
00:09:03,183 --> 00:09:05,832
They are on the patient and not in a bureau and not in a
formula he inherited.

133
00:09:05,832 --> 00:09:09,195
To use them he has to stand next to a sick person and look
at him, which is a change of profession.

134
00:09:10,489 --> 00:09:15,111
Score the colour claim first. A face carries real information,
and every physician alive still reads it.

135
00:09:15,111 --> 00:09:19,512
Pallor and jaundice and the blue of poor oxygen are the first
things anyone looks for at a bedside.

136
00:09:20,526 --> 00:09:25,516
That is a genuine hit, and it is worth being precise about
why. The chapter is not claiming that the face is pretty.

137
00:09:25,516 --> 00:09:29,474
It is claiming that the face is an instrument you can read
from right across a crowded room.

138
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:34,193
Now the pulse, and here the score splits. Rate and rhythm
and volume are real,

139
00:09:34,193 --> 00:09:39,210
and are still taken on every ward several times a day. The
correspondence with the moon is not real, and never was.

140
00:09:40,808 --> 00:09:44,823
The verdict is right instrument and wrong grid. It has come
up in almost every episode of this series,

141
00:09:44,823 --> 00:09:49,192
and it is the honest shape of what this particular tradition
actually managed to achieve, and where it stopped.

142
00:09:50,754 --> 00:09:53,204
So you have taken away my invocation and given me a
stare.

143
00:09:53,204 --> 00:09:55,739
My grandfather's physician spoke to the illness and it left.

144
00:09:55,739 --> 00:09:59,247
Mine is going to look at my face and hold my wrist and tell
me the season is wrong.

145
00:10:00,566 --> 00:10:03,767
An invocation asks the illness to leave. A sign asks it to
declare itself.

146
00:10:03,767 --> 00:10:05,930
Those are not two versions of the same profession,

147
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:09,434
and the difference between them is the only thing this
chapter is actually about.

148
00:10:10,971 --> 00:10:12,686
That is the transition, stated in one line.

149
00:10:12,686 --> 00:10:16,556
From a physician who acts on the world to one who first
requires the world to tell him something,

150
00:10:16,556 --> 00:10:19,030
and everything in medicine since has been built on the
second.

151
00:10:20,403 --> 00:10:23,055
And the chapter, having just described its greatest
advance,

152
00:10:23,055 --> 00:10:26,017
immediately says that the profession has been losing it
ever since.

153
00:10:26,017 --> 00:10:29,598
The next passage is a whole history of medicine written as
a decline, age by age.

154
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:34,126
In middle antiquity they treated an illness as it arrived.
Decoctions for ten days,

155
00:10:34,126 --> 00:10:38,816
to drive out the diseases of the eight winds and the five
blockages. The treatment began when the illness did,

156
00:10:38,816 --> 00:10:39,413
and not later.

157
00:10:40,728 --> 00:10:45,757
If ten days did not end it, they went on to the stems and
roots of herbs, using root and tip together as helpers.

158
00:10:45,757 --> 00:10:49,272
The chapter says that once root and branch were grasped,
the evil qi submitted.

159
00:10:50,747 --> 00:10:54,747
Notice the shape rather than the pharmacy. Treat early and
escalate only if that fails,

160
00:10:54,747 --> 00:10:59,253
and know which is root and which is branch before acting,
which is a modest and sensible protocol.

161
00:11:01,032 --> 00:11:05,729
In the latter age it is not like this. They do not take the four
seasons as their root or know the sun and the moon,

162
00:11:05,729 --> 00:11:08,969
nor do they stop to examine whether a thing runs with the
current or against it.

163
00:11:10,769 --> 00:11:12,835
The shape of the disease has already formed by then.

164
00:11:12,835 --> 00:11:16,410
Only then do they want a fine needle for the outside of it
and a decoction for the inside.

165
00:11:16,410 --> 00:11:19,231
They have waited until there was something large and
visible to attack.

166
00:11:20,774 --> 00:11:22,524
And here the chapter loses its composure.

167
00:11:22,524 --> 00:11:26,707
It says the crude practitioner comes on fierce and hurried
and believes the thing can be attacked,

168
00:11:26,707 --> 00:11:29,226
two characters doubled for a man in far too much of a rush.

169
00:11:30,585 --> 00:11:34,002
That is not a technical term. It is contempt, written into a
medical classic,

170
00:11:34,002 --> 00:11:38,839
and then copied out by hand for two thousand years by
people who evidently agreed that it should stay exactly

171
00:11:38,839 --> 00:11:39,416
where it was.

172
00:11:40,967 --> 00:11:44,365
And therefore the illness is not finished before a new
illness has already started.

173
00:11:44,365 --> 00:11:49,034
That is the last clause of the passage and it is the one your
physicians would least like read aloud in this room.

174
00:11:50,522 --> 00:11:55,344
Read that clause once more, slowly. The treatment causes
the next disease. That is harm done by medicine itself,

175
00:11:55,344 --> 00:11:59,478
named and written down in the Han dynasty, long before
anybody anywhere had tried to measure it.

176
00:12:00,655 --> 00:12:03,827
Hold both halves at once. The chapter is right that hurry
hurts patients.

177
00:12:03,827 --> 00:12:06,695
It is also doing exactly what it accused the present age of
doing,

178
00:12:06,695 --> 00:12:09,346
which is preferring a past that nobody can go back and
check.

179
00:12:10,483 --> 00:12:14,076
Fifth finding, and my last complaint. Three ages have gone
past and each was worse than the one before.

180
00:12:14,076 --> 00:12:17,250
If that were true of every generation since then medicine
would by now be entirely useless,

181
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:19,517
and I notice that it is not. Somebody here is grading on a
curve.

182
00:12:20,772 --> 00:12:24,103
There is one passage left, in which the Emperor asks for
the essential method,

183
00:12:24,103 --> 00:12:29,058
and what he gets back is four sentences that seem to have
almost nothing to do with anything the chapter has said so

184
00:12:29,058 --> 00:12:29,228
far.

185
00:12:31,076 --> 00:12:34,473
That is enough history, since I already know you will say
colour and pulse to me again,

186
00:12:34,473 --> 00:12:38,925
because you have said very little else for a whole hour
now, so give me the method itself and not the instruments.

187
00:12:40,770 --> 00:12:44,801
The utmost of treatment is not to lose colour and pulse, and
to use them without confusion.

188
00:12:44,801 --> 00:12:49,230
Put root and branch the wrong way round, and the spirit is
lost and the state is lost along with it.

189
00:12:50,399 --> 00:12:55,787
Then eight characters that nobody expects here. Discard
the old and take up the new, and so become a true person.

190
00:12:55,787 --> 00:12:59,601
A chapter this nostalgic ends its method by telling you to
let the old thing go.

191
00:13:01,043 --> 00:13:04,696
That is still not a method. You have given me two
instruments and a warning and a proverb.

192
00:13:04,696 --> 00:13:08,957
If there is one single thing underneath all of it that a
physician must do, then name it and I will stop.

193
00:13:10,404 --> 00:13:14,758
Shut the door and close the window. Stay with the patient.
Ask again and again after his condition,

194
00:13:14,758 --> 00:13:19,596
and follow where his own account leads. The one who
keeps his spirit flourishes and the one who loses it dies.

195
00:13:20,499 --> 00:13:24,215
Stop there, because that is the oldest description of a
clinical consultation anybody has.

196
00:13:24,215 --> 00:13:27,271
A closed room and one patient and the same question asked
again and again,

197
00:13:27,271 --> 00:13:29,501
with instructions to follow the patient's own account.

198
00:13:30,926 --> 00:13:33,632
Final finding, and then I put the tablet down. He told us the
invocation stopped working,

199
00:13:33,632 --> 00:13:37,189
and then he described a shut door and a shut window and a
man asking the same question until the patient feels heard.

200
00:13:37,189 --> 00:13:39,075
They did not stop doing that. They stopped calling it a
spell.

201
00:13:41,059 --> 00:13:45,788
He has the episode's argument, and it needs a guardrail.
Attention is part of care and is studied as part of care.

202
00:13:45,788 --> 00:13:48,942
It is not a treatment for disease, and this chapter was the
first to say so.

203
00:13:50,884 --> 00:13:54,228
A dramatized adaptation of a classical philosophical text.
Not medical advice.

204
00:13:54,228 --> 00:13:58,044
Here medicine did not stop being magic, it stopped
pretending the magic was the medicine,

205
00:13:58,044 --> 00:13:59,117
which is a smaller claim.
